1	//! Planning, as the PlanningScope says: a plain, quick list of the work
2	//! still to do, as Linear keeps issues. Each story is written as it will be
3	//! sent, a title, a prompt, and its mode, and the stories are gathered into
4	//! the next sprint and sent to the agent in order, all at once.
5	//!
6	//! The stories are kept with the project's data, in `.suspense/planning/`: a
7	//! file per story holding its hidden anchor as a queued prompt's is, with
8	//! its mode, model, effort, Slice, and attachments, and `order.json` listing
9	//! the Next sprint, Backlog, and Done sections and their stories in order,
10	//! with each story's title, whether it is a draft, and the task it was sent
11	//! as.
12	//!
13	//! [`Planning`] is the view, configured by [`PlanningHooks`]: what sending a
14	//! story does, how a sent story's task stands, and opening that task are
15	//! the application's, so the view knows nothing of the queue it sends to.
16	
